pan style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-17T09:33:32-07:00","id":483631,"title":"","content":"Pretty much everything for Wraith, but outside of it the following immediately spring to mind.<br /> <br /> Chronicle of the Black Labyrinth<br /> Book of the Wyrm<br /> Freak Legion<br /> Clanbook: Baali<br /> Dharma Book: Devil Tigers<br /> Thousand Hell's<br /> Infernalism: the Path of Screams<br /> DA: Fae<br /> Kithbook: Redcaps<br /> Kithbook: Pooka<br /> Kithbook: Nockers<br /> Nobles the Shining Host<br /> Convention Books<br /> Clanbook: Ravnos Revised<br /> Breedbook: Ratkin<br /> Breedbook: Ananasi<br /> Dreams and Nightmares<br /> Book of Madness<br /> Devil's Due<br /> <br /> And there are quite a few others following but these are the first to spring to mind. As you see I am quite fond of the darker side of the World of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T10:09:23-07:00","id":493720,"title":"","content":"Street Fighter: the Roleplaying Game <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-27T15:47:39-07:00","id":493985,"title":"","content":"The Enchanted and Nobles: The Shinning Host. A really great job creating the Changeling environment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5821-neon-sidhe","name":"Neon.Sidhe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5821_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T12:53:33-07:00","id":495102,"title":"","content":"Shadow Player's Guide saved my life. Not joking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-28T15:28:48-07:00","id":495291,"title":"","content":"Kindred of the East is an amazing book and a deeply inspired setting. I've always loved it.<br /> Mage 2nd edition was a mind opening book for me, and it inspired a lot of games and storylines and years of gametime.<br /> <br /> As for other books, I'd mark Dead Magic 2 for a brilliant look on paradigms and how to adapt different cultures into Mage. It actually helped me a lot with understanding what a paradigm actually is and how it's supposed to be. Apocalypse is the single properly done endgame book for the WoD and it really ties up the threads and concepts behind Werewolf in a brilliant and inspiring way. I'm still not tempted to run the end game, but if I did I'd surely refer to it. Tehnomancer's Toybox is loads of fun, and a lot of the items in there are fodder for whole plots and madmen. The Rokea breedbook manages to get the alienness and the coolness of the weresharks into a deeply engaging setting all of its own....<br /> <br /> ... oh come on, It's hard to pick just a few. Akashic and Euthanatos Revised Tribebooks are brilliant. The Shadow Lord tribebook and the Get of Fenris Revised make a pretty damn good case on making these two tribes feel engaging. The Sorceror's Crusade and DA:Mage (and Grimoire) take Mage in new directions, especially amazing once the pillars are introduced, Hengeyokai is just meant for fun, and it's probably one of the most fun books for the whole WoD...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}